sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/maynardsmith-hawk-dove> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis>;
    dc:description "When the cost of injury exceeds the value of the contested resource, the stable outcome is a mixture in which animals escalate with probability equal to the ratio of resource value to injury cost.";
    dc:source "John Maynard Smith (1982) Evolution and the Theory of Games";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hawk-Dove mixed ESS";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1038/246015a0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "payoffs E(H,H) = (V-C)/2, E(H,D) = V, E(D,H) = 0, E(D,D) = V/2; for C > V the unique ESS plays Hawk with probability p^* = V/C";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: symmetric pairwise contests, fixed V and C, no role asymmetries (asymmetries such as ownership give the Bourgeois ESS instead). Formal status: proved within the game.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Experimentally vary resource value and the expected cost of fighting in a contest system, and test that escalation frequency tracks V/C."
}
